---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Disclosure from '../../components/Disclosure.astro';
import EmailCapture from '../../components/EmailCapture.astro';
import { url } from '../../utils/url';
import { goHref, retailerName } from '../../data/affiliate-config';
import lightData from '../../data/lights.json';
const lights = lightData.lights;
const gaps = lightData.noParData;
const money = (n: number | null) => n == null ? 'Check current price' : `$${n.toFixed(2)} recorded`;
const headline = 'Best reef tank LED lighting: compare the data and its limits';
const itemList = { '@context':'https://schema.org', '@type':'ItemList', name:headline, numberOfItems:lights.length, itemListElement:lights.map((l,i)=>({'@type':'ListItem',position:i+1,name:`${l.brand} ${l.model}`})) };
---
<Base headline={headline} title="Best Reef Tank LED Lighting (2026)" description="Compare reef LED lights using published PAR readings, source conditions, coverage, and recorded prices. Check the limits before choosing a fixture." breadcrumbs={[{name:'Reviews',href:'/reviews'},{name:'Best Reef LED Lighting',href:'/reviews/best-reef-led-lighting'}]}>
  <section class="container tool-wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--brand-2)">Reviews · LED Lighting</p>
    <h1>{headline}</h1>
    <p class="lede-dark">Start with your tank footprint, coral placement, and a light's test conditions. A PAR reading from an air test cannot stand in for a reading under water. These four fixtures have numerical readings in our records; they were not tested side by side.</p>
    <p>Use the <a href={url('/tools/reef-par-calculator')}>reef PAR calculator</a> to explore one recorded curve at a time. Use the <a href={url('/tools/reef-build-cost-calculator')}>build cost calculator</a> to budget for the fixture count and mounting hardware your tank needs.</p>
    <Disclosure />
    <p class="rnote">Equipment prices below are recorded from {lightData.generated}, not current quotes. Source and measurement corrections were checked on {lightData.auditCheckedOn}. A change to this page does not refresh every product price. Follow the source and retailer links before ordering.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container" style="padding-top:8px">
    <h2>Four fixtures, with the conditions shown</h2>
    <div class="results">
      {lights.map((l)=>(
        <div class="rcard">
          <div class="rmain">
            <h3 class="rname">{l.brand} {l.model}</h3>
            <p class="rmeta">{l.measurementContext}</p>
            <p class="rmeta">Recorded points: {l.parCurve.map(p=>`${p.par} PAR at ${p.heightIn} inches`).join(' · ')}. <a href={l.parSource}>Read the measurement source</a>.</p>
            <p class="rmeta">{l.footprintIn} inches recorded coverage. Coverage is a maker description; it does not prove even PAR across that area.</p>
            {'wattsNote' in l && <p class="rmeta">{l.wattsNote}</p>}
            <p class="rmeta">{money(l.priceUSD)}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rbuy"><a class="aff" href={goHref(l.retailers, `${l.brand} ${l.model} reef LED light`, l.priceSource)} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">Check price at {retailerName(l.retailers)} ↗ <small>(paid link)</small></a></div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="rnote">The Orphek explorer uses only the two bottom-center readings confirmed in its linked tank test. Earlier unconfirmed points remain in the data record for audit history and are excluded from calculations. The Hydra and Fluval readings remain dated records; their sources could not be fully re-read during this check.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container prose" style="padding-top:8px">
    <h2>Which light suits your tank?</h2>
    <p><strong>A small reef:</strong> the Prime has a single manufacturer point, useful as a reference for its test depth. That one point cannot predict every mounting height. Check your tank's length and width, then leave room in the budget for a mount and a way to measure light at the corals.</p>
    <p><strong>A deeper or wider display:</strong> read the full coverage map rather than comparing its highest center number with another light. The Orphek source places its sensor on the tank bottom and changes the fixture height. A bright center does not tell you what reaches the corners.</p>
    <p><strong>A strip light:</strong> confirm the exact fixture length and output version. The Fluval record is the 46W Marine 3.0, not another size in the range. Its old retailer URL stopped working; the linked maker page identifies the model. We do not substitute another model's PAR chart or price.</p>
    <h2>Records without a comparable curve</h2>
    <p>The list below records a gap in our dataset. It does not mean a manufacturer or reviewer has never published measurements. Charts in images or videos can be useful evidence, too. Check the exact generation, spectrum, lens, intensity, sensor location, and water depth before comparing readings.</p>
    <ul>
      {gaps.map(g=>(<li><strong>{g.brand} {g.model}:</strong> {g.note} {'suitabilitySource' in g && <a href={g.suitabilitySource}>Maker's spectrum guide</a>}</li>))}
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Buying Kessil for a reef?</strong> Its <a href="https://www.kessil.com/support/choosing.php">own guide</a> identifies Tuna Blue for saltwater and Tuna Sun for freshwater. The two Tuna Sun entries above are excluded from reef buying links. Check the full variant name on the retailer page.</p>
    <h2>How to use PAR without guessing</h2>
    <p>PAR describes the light available for photosynthesis; aquarium meters commonly report photon flux density in μmol/m²/s. A useful measurement includes the fixture settings and sensor position. Moving a lamp, changing a lens, changing the water, or adding shading can change the result.</p>
    <p>The calculator interpolates only between stored points for a single fixture and reports unknown outside them. Interpolation is a straight-line estimate inside that source's setup. It does not model water absorption, lens changes, rock shadows, or a different spectrum. A single-point light gives a value only at that recorded coordinate.</p>
    <p>For your own reef, measure at the intended coral positions and change intensity gradually while watching the animals. Published tests help you choose what to investigate; they do not prove your coral receives the same light. Read <a href={url('/how-we-rate')}>our methods</a>, then plan water movement with the <a href={url('/tools/flow-calculator')}>flow calculator</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container"><EmailCapture /></section>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(itemList)} />
</Base>
